id: pm-2f80fn
title: "The changelog drift check reports that the changelog is out of date without naming what drifted, so an order-only diff is indistinguishable from a release-attribution defect"
description: "changelog generate --check exits 1 with only the file path; it never reports which sections changed, which items moved, or whether membership changed at all. The two causes require opposite responses, so every closed-item mutation reads as equally dangerous and the terminal-record enrichment programme has been deferred behind a diagnostic that already computed the answer and discarded it."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 1
tags[5]: agent-ux,changelog,diagnostics,release,token-efficiency
created_at: "2026-08-10T12:11:45.027Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-10T12:15:36.569Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: "The drift refusal reports whether any item entered or left the changelog, as an explicit boolean, not inferred from counts; The refusal names the affected release sections and a bounded sample of moved rows with before and after positions; Counts come first and the sample is capped, so the diagnostic stays within the command output budget; A regeneration whose only difference is intra-section row order is reported as order-only in the refusal text"
goal: Agent-legible diagnostics
objective: Make a drift refusal actionable from the refusal alone
value: Retires the do-not-touch-closed-items convention by letting an agent see that a diff is order-only
impact: Blocks the terminal-record graph enrichment programme and every closed-item metadata burn-down behind it
outcome: A drift refusal distinguishes membership change from row reordering and is actionable without a manual diff
why_now: Measured 2026-08-10 while establishing whether historical graph enrichment is changelog-safe; the check was the only thing that could not answer
reviewer: maintainer-review
risk: low
confidence: high
sprint: 2026-w33
reporter: maintainer-agent
severity: medium
environment: "pm 2026.8.10, pm-changelog 2026.8.7, 2017 changelog items"
repro_steps: "Run changelog:pm:check on a clean tree; add one dependency row to a long-closed item; run changelog:pm:check again"
expected_result: "The refusal names whether membership changed, which sections moved, and a bounded sample of moved rows"
actual_result: "The refusal names only the output path, so the agent must regenerate to a scratch path and diff by hand to learn anything"
component: pm-changelog changelog generate --check
